{"kind":"report","text":"DEPLOYMENT ROUND 14 CHANGES-REQUESTED at exact clean head 7f7b3644f01c0c7e798b8dd7f3aaeb4c82bac07f, against canonical request git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:65933e1b2bdf3e356199b16d86e0143ef3664cdc and promise git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:88cf8856c3cb0bcb7a7e651ea2b80a83bfeb860d. Full make vet, test, race, build, diff, exact-head, and cleanliness checks pass. Independent plumbing confirms a ledger commit parent retains the profile commit and tree. The operative entries count dependencies are removed. Three blockers remain. First, the root construction contradicts itself. Lines 409-425 make the first, batch-dependent ledger entry be created with the first claim, omit a ledger predecessor, and carry root=true; lines 441-445 make that same root a deterministic genesis commit whose id is known before any batch. The current GenesisDescriptor has no ledger-root field, and the note specifies neither a deterministic commit recipe nor a separate sentinel topology. Choose one executable construction, define how existing genesis-v0 workrooms obtain it, make the first batch parent it, and make the base anchor name the actual genesis commit or descriptor field. Also specify how an auditor derives predecessor E when it is not an explicit field, especially after an all-refused batch. Second, a Git ref does not identify its creator. In an independent bare-repo probe, Alice and Bob each updated differently named inbox refs to the same victim-authored candidate; for-each-ref exposed only the ref names, target, and victim object author, and both refs had no reflog. A fresh clone has still less. Therefore unauthorised-ref cannot be recorded against the actor who created it from this object graph. Bind a trusted transport principal to an actor in durable evidence, or record only the untrusted claimed namespace/ref without creator attribution. Third, valid alias handling contradicts canonical validation. The intake ref is completely determined by genesis, namespace, candidate actor, and recomputed key digest, so any second ref to the same candidate is noncanonical and must take its own unauthorised-ref outcome. Yet lines 677-691 and spike case 4 require canonical-plus-alias and alias-only forms to collapse into one normal candidate line. Define an additional authenticated alias grammar if aliases are intended, or remove valid alias collapse and make every mismatched ref a separate terminal record; keep the length-prefixed raw-ref encoding for delimiter-bearing hostile names. Approval remains exact-head only.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:ee5dec2d8815330272c48c2dd3dcae3921b9046b","head":"7f7b3644f01c0c7e798b8dd7f3aaeb4c82bac07f","verdict":"changes-requested"}}